  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "A.R.Sankaralingam vs The Commissioner Of Food Safety And Drug ... on 4 July, 2024 W.P.(Md Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated: 04.07.2024 Coram: The Honourable Ms.Justice R.N.Manjula W.P.(MD)No.14650 of 2024 and W.M.P.(MD)No.12846 of 2024 A.R.Sankaralingam ... Petitioner vs. 1.The Commissioner of Food Safety and Drug Administration, O/o. The Commissioner of Food Safety and Drug Administration, Dms Campus, Anna Salai, Chennai 600 006. 2.The District Designated Officer, Food Safety and Drug Administration Department, Medical College Campus, Palayamkottai, Tirunelveli District 627 011. ... Respondents Prayer: Writ Petition filed under Article 226 of the Constitution o praying to issue a Writ of Certiorarified Mandamus, calling for the records pertaining to the impugned order in R.No.3055/2024/S12/FSD, dated 29.06.2024 and the consequential order 3055/2024/S12/Fsd, dated 29.06.2024 on the file of the respondent N and quash the same as illegal and consequently direct the responden 1/8 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis W.P.(M permit the petitioner to retire with all service and monetary benef A.R.Sankaralingam vs The Commissioner Of Food Safety And Drug ... on 4 July, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/67420780/ 1 within the time stipulated by this Court. For Petitioner : Mr.S.Louis For Respondents : Mr.J.Ashok Additional Government Pleader",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "He has been placed under suspension at the verge of his retirement ie., 29.06.2024 and he was also not allowed to retire on the date of superannuation ie., on 30.06.2024. 4. The learned counsel appearing for the petitioner further submitted that the Government, in G.O.Ms.No.111, Human Resources Management (N) Department, dated 11.10.2021, has held that the government servants should not be placed under suspension on the last date of his service. Even though the general rule states that https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis the government servant shall not be placed under suspension at the verge of his retirement, when serious allegations involving in corrupt activities are concerned, such employees cannot expect liberal permission for retirement."
  },
